# The primitive table of the translator (§GATE "all settings in tables", slice 2; Q36, Q41;
# steps/table-receiver.md §7): the profile derived from lingvamyxa_prev's `primitive.description` (lm2/primitive.lm2).
# The translator reads the columns class, cell and convert (l2_prim_kind): a row names a
# primitive, `cell` 1 is a cell primitive, `convert` forbidden forbids a conversion to or from it.
# The active profile includes the original 23 rows and the C99/profile aliases needed by declaration descriptions.
# Ten additional rows are retained verbatim from lingvamyxa_prev/lm2/primitive.lm2; schar describes signed char,
# and _Bool explicitly shares bool's contract. Recognition is separate from implemented storage/lowering.
# Other legacy semantic/library rows are not imported merely because the old catalog contains them:
# Cell Count Integer Flag Ratio Float Complex Atom Address Opaque Text usize isize categoryFlag bigint real decimal DecimalText.
# Where the translator's tables live is open (Q46); until then this file is read beside the source, as
# convert.lm2 is.
table:
    source
    name: `primitive.description`
    columns: (class: class) (categoryFlag: cell) (class: semantic) (categoryFlag: numeric) (categoryFlag: integer) (categoryFlag: floating) (categoryFlag: reference) (categoryFlag: opaque) (categoryFlag: callable) (categoryFlag: descriptor) (categoryFlag: signed) (class: width) (class: range) (class: spelling) (class: convert)
    rows:
             None     0  none    0  0  0  0  0  0  0  0  None      None                     void            forbidden
             void     0  none    0  0  0  0  0  0  0  0  None      None                     void            forbidden
             char     1  integer 1  1  0  0  0  0  0  1  profile   "C99-char(profile)"      char            keyed
             schar    1  integer 1  1  0  0  0  0  0  1  profile   "SCHAR_MIN..SCHAR_MAX(profile)" "signed char" keyed
             short    1  integer 1  1  0  0  0  0  0  1  profile   "C99-short(profile)"     short           keyed
             int      1  integer 1  1  0  0  0  0  0  1  profile   "C99-int(profile)"       int             keyed
             long     1  integer 1  1  0  0  0  0  0  1  profile   "C99-long(profile)"      long            keyed
